{"title":"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two vertical trees are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> m and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m tall. The bases of the trees are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m apart along horizontal ground. A bird flies from the top of the shorter tree to the top of the taller tree along a straight path at a constant speed of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> m/s. How long does it take the bird to complete the flight?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that the sides form a trapezium/trapezoid, so we can label the different vertices and draw a perpendicular line from the side with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5dbe54826bd5c1c29c57f0dbc9fd637425f0602c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to the side with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27acd04b639e953161234b726233dd34257cbf3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />, forming a rectangle and a triangle:\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Opposite sides of a rectangle are equal in length, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> has a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75d2529d7591028c84086cf7738e9cc43ce25f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783d500281f8f46167dff3b071c543d42150e67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DP$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> has a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5dbe54826bd5c1c29c57f0dbc9fd637425f0602c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e049532148caaf1c48e37658b548a6255c8d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783d500281f8f46167dff3b071c543d42150e67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DP$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> form side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, so the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e049532148caaf1c48e37658b548a6255c8d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/854d849d612b38906440b9bbdcb1aaf8d42d8d64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 - 5 = 10 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">pythagorean theorem</a>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/6950c559356bbeaed2872a18d562ccdbeeb6eeae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^{2} = PC^{2} + AP^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c5705c9ae3bf732d2733fb761adbdfb752b939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^{2} = 10^{2} + 24^{2} = 100 + 576$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"236\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d64b61de98c57cadc43ae6a5287bd55f1423c12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^{2} = 676$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f0079ca753ce47f5490d2e6ed4302ef672c68cdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\sqrt{676} = 26 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Since the bird goes along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at a constant speed of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6cac1dea3a3dfdf1d88a48395c87b079a0b6f09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, it takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421fa92d9fc07357edbe51f98608f850f4b4e825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{26}{4} = \\boxed{\\frac{13}{2} \\text{ s}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"94\" height=\"49\" /> to complete the flight.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC\" title=\"2024 CSMC\">2024 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065715\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 144/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1968/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3934/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion 